## PHASE 1 — Foundation, truth & hygiene
**Maps brief phases: 0, 42, 43, 48, 49, 51 (partial), 58 (audit part)**

Make the repo honest before adding anything.

- [x] Full-repo audit (4 parallel deep audits — matrix above)
- [ ] Remove stale/wrong docs: delete `docs/tech-stack.md` (describes a product
      that never shipped: Stripe, Node CLI, WebSocket, mock phase), rewrite
      `docs/architecture.md` (lists pages that don't exist: passports/rescue/code)
- [ ] Fix stale doc claims: `CONTRIBUTING.md` (Go tests DO exist; web tests live
      in `lib/`), `API.md` (`POST /api/chat/:id/switch`, not `PATCH .../model`;
      no `POST /api/chat/:id/memory`), `PRODUCT-STATUS.md` (17 models, not 21)
- [ ] Delete dead/junk: `lib/data/workspace.ts`, `lib/data/prompts.ts` (unimported
      mock datasets), empty `packages/config/` + `packages/ui/`, empty
      `apps/api/src/services/{analytics,marketing}/`, tracked legacy
      `.eslintrc.json`, `.dockerignore` `mlflow.org` line, Dockerfile fly.toml
      comments, `terminal/test/` empty dirs, `.DS_Store`, `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`
- [ ] Demote Rescue to an import utility in nav/copy (it already is in the
      sidebar; root `package.json` description still leads with it)
- [ ] Keep useful features (improve, cost estimates, continue packs) — integrate,
      never delete (they are already integrated into chat/rescue)

**Acceptance:** every doc describes the actual repo; `grep -r "mock\|placeholder\|TODO"`
in production code returns only intentional test/demo markers.

## PHASE 2 — Chat actually works (the headline fix)
**Maps brief phases: 3, 4, 6 (failover part), 52 (web leg)**

- [x] Diagnose: all provider keys dead/hanging; no per-call timeout → infinite hang
- [ ] **Provider watchdog** (chat router `runSingleCall`, runs execute, gateway):
      abort if no first delta in ~25s, abort if stream idles ~45s, mark key
      `provider_timeout` (cooldown) so failover skips it — a hanging endpoint
      must fail over, never hang the UI
- [ ] **Model registry truth**: add `openai/gpt-oss-120b` ($0.15/$0.60 per 1M,
      cached $0.075) and `openai/gpt-oss-20b` ($0.075/$0.30, cached $0.0375) for
      Groq; swap the deprecated `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` out of every priority
      chain (chat, improve, rescue, agents, memory-extract) and the web picker
- [ ] E2E proof: signup → session → message → streamed reply → persisted →
      usage ledger row (verified via curl SSE + DB)
- [ ] Context pipeline audit already REAL (provider isolation, last-8 verbatim,
      Redis-cached summaries, memory retrieval, token budget) — keep, add tests

**Acceptance:** with exactly one healthy provider key, chat replies end-to-end;
with a hanging provider, chat fails over within one watchdog window.

## PHASE 3 — Model system: one registry, one truth
**Maps brief phases: 5, 6, 7, 29 (cache part), 38, 54**

- [ ] Web consumes `@layerflow/model-registry` directly (kill the fiction catalog
      in `lib/data/providers.ts` that lists gpt-5 / claude-opus-4.5 / deepseek-v3 —
      models the platform cannot serve)
- [ ] Chat model picker: keep static fallback but drive from `/api/models`
      (new session-auth endpoint: registry + live availability) so the picker
      never offers unservable models
- [ ] Router AUTO policy: task-type heuristics exist (`intelligence/route.ts`) —
      verify coding/reasoning/large-context routing actually picks differently
- [ ] Provider health: key-health table exists — add per-provider latency rolling
      stats into routing decisions
- [ ] Multi-model test matrix: Auto / provider A / provider B / unavailable /
      BYOK — assert model ID, provider, tokens, cost, fallback event

**Acceptance:** exactly one model definition source (the registry); the Models
page and picker show only servable models; fallback emits `switched` events.

## PHASE 4 — Usage, budgets, observability
**Maps brief phases: 8, 9, 29, 31, 46**

- [x] Budget reserve/settle via Redis Lua + immutable usage_ledger — REAL, keep
- [ ] Verify reservation release on every failure path (chat settle-failure
      path releases; audit gateway + runs for the same)
- [ ] Structured logs have request IDs — add job IDs to every worker log line
      and provider latency metrics per model
- [ ] Costs page: replace client-side `providerForModel` prefix-guessing with
      server-provided provider on usage rows
- [ ] Perf: add tenant indexes where queries filter without one; kill N+1s in
      progress endpoints (verify with EXPLAIN on hot routes)

**Acceptance:** every AI call produces a ledger row with user/workspace/session/
provider/model/tokens/cost; failed reservations never leak budget headroom.

## PHASE 5 — Agents become real execution systems
**Maps brief phases: 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16, 40, 53**

The biggest honest gap: agents are prompt→LLM with **zero tools**; job listings
are model-invented fiction; `agent_templates` table is unused (13 hardcoded).

- [ ] Typed agent state machine: PLAN → ACT → OBSERVE → DECIDE → VERIFY → DONE
      with max-iterations + timeout (today: one LLM call per run)
- [ ] **Server-side tool framework** (v1: read_file, search_files, write_file,
      edit_file, run_command sandboxed, web_search, fetch_url, create_report) —
      the terminal already has a complete-but-dead Go tool engine to port the
      permission model from
- [ ] Tool permission policy per agent (read=open, write=approval,
      shell=approval, destructive=explicit) — `agent_permissions` table exists
- [ ] Structured events: agent_started/planning/tool_requested/tool_approved/
      tool_started/tool_completed/assistant_delta/paused/failed/completed →
      persist to `agent_steps` + stream via SSE (today: polling snapshot)
- [ ] Structured output artifacts (leads/reports/applications) with table/CSV/
      JSON export; `artifacts` table + storage; PDF generation in the worker
      (library: e.g. pdfkit) → R2/local storage → secure download link
- [ ] Job agent honesty: stop presenting invented listings as found jobs —
      either real search sources (APIs the user configures) or clearly-labeled
      "model-suggested targets" with user review before any outreach
- [ ] Resume parsing: real extraction (today: client regex heuristics; PDFs
      never parsed) — move to worker with a proper parser

**Acceptance:** a coding agent inspects a repo, proposes a diff, waits for
approval, applies it, and the run + steps + approvals persist and stream.

## PHASE 6 — Terminal is first-class
**Maps brief phases: 19, 20, 21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26, 55, 56, 57**

Critical bugs found (with fixes queued):

- [ ] **Stream pump re-arm** (`tui/chat.go` `streamCmd` + `app.go`): return the
      next read Cmd from every `streamChunkMsg` — TUI chat currently stalls
      after the first token
- [ ] **Render toasts** (`app.go` `renderToasts` has zero call sites — 36
      pushToast calls are invisible)
- [ ] **Sync pull fix**: `sync.go` pulls with the SERVER watermark (always
      empty) — pull with the LOCAL watermark; materialize pulled ops into
      `sessions`/`messages`; add JSON tags (payloads currently marshal with
      capitalized Go field names); journal TUI sessions too (only `lf chat`
      CLI journals today)
- [ ] Rune-safe truncation (4 sites slice bytes mid-rune → mojibake)
- [ ] One theme: replace glamour `dracula` (blue/purple) with an orange/gray
      chroma style; purge ad-hoc ANSI colors in `tui/diff.go`, `approval.go`
- [ ] Layout: fixed composer slot (viewport currently recomputes against
      growing composer height → jumping); stop re-centering home on every
      render; stop mutating state inside `View()`
- [ ] Wire the dead subsystems: tools+permission+sandbox (agent safety),
      `search.Build()` (FTS index never built), `memory.InitSchema()` (never
      called — table name mismatch), daemon indexer (never assigned)
- [ ] Tool sandboxing: `resolvePath` has no containment (path traversal passes),
      `run_command` has no dangerous-command block/timeout — fix before wiring
- [ ] `lf doctor` auth false-negative for pasted platform keys; `/model`+
      `/provider` slash commands mutate only a discarded context
- [ ] Stub honesty: `mcp add/remove/health`, `sessions --open` either ship or
      print "not available" (they do) — keep until Phase 5 tools land
- [ ] Transport: SSE is fine for v2 (brief allows REST+SSE for CRUD; WS for
      streaming) — add reconnect+resume for the TUI stream (local state
      retention + dedupe on resume)

**Acceptance:** `lf` TUI streams a full reply without stalling; a web session
appears in `lf sessions` after `lf sync`; no blue/purple anywhere; `go vet` +
`go test -race` clean.

## PHASE 7 — Memory, search, context engine
**Maps brief phases: 17, 18, 27, 28, 33, 41**

- [ ] Memory pipeline is REAL (extract job, dedupe, pgvector) — extend types
      (decisions, project facts) and add terminal memory sync (schema exists,
      never synced)
- [ ] Search: extend beyond prompts+sessions to memories, files, agent runs,
      artifacts (hybrid keyword+vector, tenant-scoped)
- [ ] Repo context: detect package manifests, build a project context index,
      relevance-select files within token budget (never dump the repo)
- [ ] One shared context engine for web + terminal + agents (web path is solid;
      terminal has its own dead `internal/context` — unify or port)
- [ ] File uploads: presigned R2 exists — add content-type sniffing (never
      trust extensions), size limits, and tenant-scoped download URLs

**Acceptance:** "continue the auth work" resolves the right project, session,
memories, and files in both web and terminal.

## PHASE 8 — Web frontend truth
**Maps brief phases: 35, 36, 37, 39 (partial), 51**

- [ ] Models hub: real registry data (Phase 3) — remove fiction catalog
- [ ] Billing: wire to `GET /api/billing/status` (exists, never called); delete
      hardcoded `PLANS`/`INVOICES`/"Payments simulated" or gate behind
      billing-configured
- [ ] Settings: wire profile/preferences saves or remove fake buttons
      ("Export all data", "Delete workspace", cosmetic saves, mock-data text)
- [ ] Prompts: remove hardcoded sub-scores (94/92/90…) and `score: 50` mapper
      defaults; wire favorite star to the API; wire or remove "Run" button
- [ ] Dead buttons: "Use for routing" (models), "Edit project" (workspace) —
      wire or remove
- [ ] Workspace stats: `projectCount/promptCount` mappers return 0 — compute real
- [ ] Nav priority: Chat, Terminal, Agents first (current: Home, Chat, then
      Build group — close; reorder)
- [ ] Every section keeps loading/empty/error/retry states (already good)

**Acceptance:** no fake numbers anywhere; every button does something real or
is gone.

## PHASE 9 — Security hardening
**Maps brief phases: 1 (CLI auth), 32, 12 (permission bypass)**

- [ ] Audit pass: tenant isolation on every route (spot-check IDOR on
      session/message/file/artifact lookups), CSRF posture, rate limits
- [ ] Terminal tools: path containment, command allow/block, timeout, env
      filtering (before Phase 6 wiring)
- [ ] Prompt-injection: tool inputs validated; approvals cannot be bypassed by
      model output
- [ ] Secrets: never logged (verify adapter error paths don't echo keys);
      BYOK ciphertext never returned (already tested)
- [ ] SSRF on fetch_url/web_search tools (Phase 5) — allowlist, no private IPs

**Acceptance:** security checklist in `docs/SECURITY.md` verified item by item.

## PHASE 10 — Testing, deployment, launch verdict
**Maps brief phases: 44, 45, 47, 50, 58, 59, 60**

- [ ] E2E flows (brief's 7): signup→chat→persistence; login→session→model
      switch→stream→cost; agent create→run→tool→approval→result; job agent with
      resume; web↔terminal session continuation; PDF→worker→storage→download;
      lf login→chat→sync
- [ ] Failure tests: provider timeout, invalid key, model unavailable, rate
      limit, Redis down, Postgres down, worker restart, WS/SSE disconnect,
      malformed tool input, cross-workspace access, expired session, duplicate
      events/jobs, agent timeout, budget exceeded
- [ ] CI: add root `npm test` + `eslint` + `go test -race` to ci.yml (today CI
      skips all three)
- [ ] Production: Render (API+worker) + Vercel (web) + Neon + Upstash + R2 —
      configs exist and are consistent; run `check:prod` + smoke against prod
- [ ] Write `docs/PRODUCTION_AUDIT.md` with the required table + honest verdict
      (READY FOR PRIVATE BETA / PUBLIC BETA / NOT READY)

**Acceptance:** all critical user journeys pass in CI; verdict backed by
evidence, not vibes.

